  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Saturday)\nIssued at 1226 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nCloud cover is progged to scatter out during the day Sunday while\nsurface high pressure filters into the region. At the same time,\nlight northerly winds are anticipated Sunday with high\ntemperatures in the 70s to low 80s forecast. These conditions\ncontinue Monday with the southern Plains on the eastern periphery\nof a ridge of high pressure centered over the Desert Southwest.\nLight winds and mostly clear skies Sunday night and again Monday\nnight will aid in low temperatures falling into the 50s for most\nlocations. There is some potential for fog development again\nSunday night/early Monday morning while surface high pressure is\nover the region. \n\nWinds begin to transition back out of the south mid week with the\nridge of high pressure out west trying to expand eastward over the\nsouthern Plains. This pattern looks to begin a warming trend with\nhigh temperatures climbing back above seasonal average through \nthe second half of the week. Latest model solutions differ late \nweek into next weekend, though a signal suggests a potential for a\nreturn of showers with an area of low pressure developing/lifting\nnortheast over the southern Plains. Will continue to keep PoPs \nbelow mentionable criteria at the end of the forecast period, \nthough its something to watch over the week ahead.",
